# The secret-value pattern. A reader of this file refuses to send text or a
# file whose bytes match it anywhere. It judges the value, never the words
# around it, so `secrets=22 plain=0`, `tokens=` and a `"secret":` key are
# clean. It is written for the fleet's `fleet-state-sync` gate and the
# `slack` package, before a post or a file upload; `fleet-state-sync` keeps
# its own copy until it reads this one. kendex's leaked-key audit keeps a
# separate prefix list, `crates/core/src/quality/secret.rs`. A rule on a
# secret word's name and its value is the reader's own; this file holds value
# shapes alone: a private-key header, and a GitHub, `sk-` or Slack token
# prefix followed by the key characters, with no letter, digit or `_` before
# the prefix.
#
# Dialect: POSIX extended regular expression, in the subset Python's `re`
# reads with the same meaning. Flags: case-insensitive, bytes in the C
# locale. A match is a refusal. Read it one of these ways:
#
#   shell   LC_ALL=C grep -aiE -e "$pattern" FILE     (exit 0 is a match)
#   Python  re.compile(pattern.encode(), re.I | re.M).search(data)
#
# `re.M` is required: grep matches line by line, so `^` is a line start there
# and must be one in Python too.
#
# The pattern is the one line below that is neither empty nor a `#` comment.
# A reader that finds no such line, or more than one, refuses.

-----BEGIN [A-Z ]*PRIVATE KEY-----|(^|[^A-Za-z0-9_])(gh[pousr]_[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}|github_pat_[A-Za-z0-9_]{20,}|sk-[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}|xox[baprs]-[A-Za-z0-9-]{10,}|xapp-[A-Za-z0-9-]{10,})
